…take their places below. A toast is offered to the ruler; after the ruler raises the general toast and circulates the return toast, a toast is offered to the high ministers. Once they raise the general toast and circulate the return toast, a toast is offered to the grand masters. After the grand masters raise the general toast [and circulate the return toast], a toast is offered to the servicemen. After the servicemen raise the general toast and circulate the return toast, a toast is offered to the sons of noblemen. The positions all have graded distinctions, by which noble and base are made clear.

Patent of Appointment for a Hanlin Academician (Hanlin xueshi) [?].

Memorial by [Xing] Bing [? — transcribed □佑] Thanking Emperor Zhenzong for Visiting the Temple of Culture-Propagating King (Wenxuan miao).

[Legal Judgments on Five] Statutes [? — transcribed □程]:
[Privately Manufacturing] Hu, Dou, Steelyards, and Foot-Measures;
Profaning the Spirits and Gods;
Detaining and Causing Difficulties at [Fords and] Passes;
Manufacturing Not in Accordance with the Regulations.
